      "message": "Thanks for bringing this up.\n\nAfter a deeper inspection, I do not think this change is required at all:\n`GPIO_OUTPUT_INACTIVE` includes `GPIO_OUTPUT_INIT_LOGICAL` see [gpio.h:71](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h;l\u003d71?q\u003dzephyr%2Fmain%2Finclude%2Fzephyr%2Fdrivers%2Fgpio.h\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch)which along with `GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW` (this last one passed by DT using `intel,ap-pwrseq-gpio`) it will set output GPIO to the correct level during initialization, see [gpio.h:993](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h;l\u003d993?q\u003dzephyr%2Fmain%2Finclude%2Fzephyr%2Fdrivers%2Fgpio.h\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch).",
